WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.940
We all know that "When you play the game of

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.780
thrones, you win or you die.”
So, I’m going to run through my top 10 deaths

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.130
from season 4.
I’m only including deaths which we actually

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:18.539
saw on screen – so no Rast dying by direwolf
and no death by giant for Grenn.

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:23.199
Also, I’m only covering the deaths of named
characters – so, for example, while the

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:29.029
episode 9 death of random wild-lings by scythe…
or big-ass anchor, as I like to call it…

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.300
was undeniably very cool, it hasn’t made
it to my list.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.769
Just before I kick off, if it’s your first
time here, I’ve got exclusive interviews

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:42.970
with the Game of Thrones cast, weekly reviews
of the latest episodes, and more top GoT lists.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:48.979
So, if you haven’t already, do subscribe!
Ok, let’s countdown the top 10 deaths in

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:50.010
Season 4!

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.979
It was always going to be a bittersweet moment
when red-headed Wild-ling Ygritte saw her

00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:00.420
former lover Jon Snow again.
And so it was when the pair locked eyes as

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.250
the battle of Castle Black raged around them.
Last time they saw each other was when Ygritte

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.790
shot Jon in the back.
And this time, she had her arrow trained on

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.890
him again as he looked at her fondly and she
struggled to reconcile her love for him with

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.790
her allegiance to the Wild-lings.
But, the decision was taken out of her hands

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:23.130
when orphaned potato boy, Olly, raised his
own arrow and shot Ygritte from behind right

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.720
through her heart.
Just as our favourite Wild-ling had shot Olly’s

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.100
dad in the back of the head when the Wildlings
raided their village in episode 3.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.610
As she died in Jon’s arms, she wished they’d
stayed in the cave, and said, one last time,

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.720
“You know nothing, Jon Snow”.
If you still miss Ygritte, check out this

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.150
video to see the Game of Thrones cast and
fans do their best impressions of her classic

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:47.290
line.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:53.520
Jon Snow was really up against it in the Battle
of Castle Black when he came face-to-face

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.600
with the insanely strong tower of a man, Styr,
the Magnar of Thenn.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.560
Styr used his huge battleaxe to knock Jon’s
sword out of his hands before Jon got his

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.820
hands on a chain and used it to wrangle Styr’s
battleaxe off him.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:12.380
Then the pair went mano-a-mano, with Jon getting
SMASHED against an anvil.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:17.500
But as Styr looked set to go in for the kill,
Jon proved he’d learned a thing or two from

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.750
Karl Tanner about not always fighting honourably.
Yes, just as Karl did to him at Craster’s

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:27.920
Keep, Jon spat in Styr’s face and used the
distraction to grab a hefty hammer which he

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:34.330
smashed into Styr’s bald head.
No more roast crow for you, Mr Thenn!

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:39.569
Episode 5 saw Locke – the man who lopped
off Jaime Lannister’s hand – rock up at

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:44.260
Craster’s Keep with Jon Snow and a bunch
of Night’s Watch men to take down Karl Tanner

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.400
and the other rebellious former rangers holed
up there.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:53.550
But unbeknown to our Men in Black, Locke was
actually only there to accomplish his mission

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.500
of hunting down Bran and Rickon Stark for
Roose Bolton!

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.080
And when he found Bran and his friends in
a hut outside Craster’s Keep, Locke showed

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.160
he’s still got a bit of a thing about limbs
as he cut Bran’s leg to check he really

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.630
was the paralysed Stark boy!
But as Locke carted the young Stark off, Bran

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:16.739
warged into Hodor and turned him into Warg-dor,
or should that be Bran-dor, anyway, he was

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:22.950
basically a not-so-gentle giant who went all
Incredible Hulk on Locke’s ass, snapping

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:28.129
the House Bolton man’s neck!
Let that be a lesson to anyone who calls Hodor

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:28.950
an idiot!
But did you see that look on poor Hodor’s

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.950
You can watch my interviews with actor Noah
Taylor, who played Locke, and Kristian Nairn,

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.120
who plays Hodor, here.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.239
He may have killed creepy Craster, but rebellious
ranger Karl Tanner certainly kept the “eep”

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:46.030
in Craster’s Keep, violating the dead wild-ling’s
daughter-wives and sending what he thought

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:50.569
was his last son to the White Walkers.
So, despite being a “fooking legend” in

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:55.500
his own mind, it was always quite clear that
Karl was not long for this Game of Thrones

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.879
world.
Still, he went out fighting – even if he

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:03.400
did use some dirty tactics – and almost
proved Oberyn Martell’s wise words that

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.540
“long swords are a bad option in close quarters”
during his face-off with Jon Snow inside Craster’s

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.959
Keep.
In fact, it was only thanks to one of Craster’s

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:12.500
women stabbing Karl in the back that Jon was
able to get back on

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:17.530
his feet, after being tripped up by Karl,
and run his sword through the back of Karl’s

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.199
head and right out of his
mouth!

00:04:19.199 --> 00:04:24.139
A fitting end for the man who drank wine from
the skull of Lord Commander Mormont, and,

00:04:24.139 --> 00:04:30.469
an end, which also, mirrored the way Podrick
saved Tyrion at Blackwater.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:35.279
Remember Polliver? Yeah, that’s right, the
Lannister man who stole Arya’s sword Needle

00:04:35.279 --> 00:04:39.819
and used it to murder Lommy Greenhands, the
young kid travelling north on the Kingsroad

00:04:39.819 --> 00:04:44.589
with Arya, Gendry, Hot Pie and Yoren.
Well, they say that revenge is a dish best

00:04:44.589 --> 00:04:49.849
served cold and Arya finally got hers when
she came across Polliver at the Inn at the

00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:54.529
Crossroads, took back Needle and stuck him
with the pointy end, polishing him off by

00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:59.870
running the sword right through his throat.
This death scene proved a satisfying payback

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.789
for Polliver’s actions in season 2, and
a strong end to the opening episode of season

00:05:04.789 --> 00:05:07.400
4.
Melisandre was certainly right when she foresaw

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.159
darkness in Arya towards the end of season
2.

00:05:10.159 --> 00:05:16.589
By the way, you can check out my latest interview
with Maisie Williams, who plays Arya, here!

00:05:16.589 --> 00:05:21.210
If anyone had actually dared to ask Tywin
Lannister how he’d like to exit the world

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:26.490
of Westeros, you can be pretty sure he would
not have said: “sitting on the toilet in

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:31.559
a brief break from sex with a prostitute”.
But, ultimately, even the all-powerful papa

00:05:31.559 --> 00:05:36.729
Lannister didn’t always get what he wanted.
So, Tywin’s letter-writing days were brought

00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:41.279
to an end by a crossbow on the crapper.
And, as if that wasn’t enough insult added

00:05:41.279 --> 00:05:45.159
to injury, the King’s Hand died at the hands
of his own son, Tyrion.

00:05:45.159 --> 00:05:49.789
Still, it was quite something seeing Tywin
do his very best to maintain the upper hand

00:05:49.789 --> 00:05:55.110
in his conversation with Tyrion, in spite
of his, erm, somewhat delicate position.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:06:00.490
And, contrary to popular belief about the
Lannisters’ incredible wealth, Tywin did

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:04.969
not, in the end, shit gold.
Still, now the Lannister legacy can boast

00:06:04.969 --> 00:06:11.969
both a king-slayer and a kin-slayer! Go lions!
To see where daddy Lannister’s death ranks

00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:18.050
in Tywin’s TOP 10 on-screen moments, check
out my countdown here!

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:23.319
Season 4 of Game of Thrones reminded us that,
if you fancy living a long life, it’s probably

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:29.649
best NOT to RSVP to any weddings invitations,
especially if you’re the one due to get

00:06:29.649 --> 00:06:32.379
hitched!
Yes, the Lannisters’ moto may be ‘Hear

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:37.969
Me roar’, but it was more a case of ‘Hear
Me croak’ in episode 2 as young King Joffrey

00:06:37.969 --> 00:06:44.339
drew his last breath after scoffing some particularly
dry pigeon pie and washing that down with

00:06:44.339 --> 00:06:48.149
some poisoned wine.
Thanks to Cersei, all eyes in King’s Landing

00:06:48.149 --> 00:06:53.199
were on Tyrion as the culprit; but in reality
it was Littlefinger and Olenna Tyrell, helped

00:06:53.199 --> 00:06:57.740
by Dontos and an unwitting Sansa.
There’s no doubt that Joffrey was the thorn

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.929
in everyone’s side – except his adoring
mother’s – since the start of the show,

00:07:02.929 --> 00:07:08.809
and he was malicious to the very last, with
jibes at everyone in his firing line including

00:07:08.809 --> 00:07:12.849
Sansa and Tyrion.
Yet he was such a fantastic character played

00:07:12.849 --> 00:07:17.569
so brilliantly by Jack Gleeson, and we did
love to hate Joffrey so much, that it was

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:21.839
almost a shame to see him finally felled.
By the way, you can check out what the Game

00:07:21.839 --> 00:07:28.339
of Thrones cast had to say about Joffrey and
actor Jack Gleeson in this video.

00:07:28.339 --> 00:07:34.149
No matter how crazy you think your relatives
are, they’ve probably got nothing on Lysa

00:07:34.149 --> 00:07:37.379
Arryn.
Why? Because this is the woman best known

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:41.839
for threatening to throw Tyrion out of the
moon door for murdering her husband Jon Arryn

00:07:41.839 --> 00:07:47.619
despite having poisoned him herself, almost
breaking her niece Sansa’s fingers as she

00:07:47.619 --> 00:07:53.149
interrogated her about sleeping with Littlefinger,
ear-piercingly noisy sex with her new husband

00:07:53.149 --> 00:07:59.069
Petyr Baelish, and, oh yeah, breast-feeding
her fully-grown son, Robin.

00:07:59.069 --> 00:08:05.289
Anyway, Mrs Littlefinger was very obviously
cruising for a bruising as we know only too

00:08:05.289 --> 00:08:10.419
well that Littlefinger does not like leaving
people alive who can reveal his secrets, as

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:15.439
Ros and Dontos discovered the hard way.
So, when Lysa threatened to toss Sansa out

00:08:15.439 --> 00:08:20.839
of the moon door after catching her kissing
Littlefinger, it gave him the perfect opportunity

00:08:20.839 --> 00:08:24.889
to create some more chaos by giving his new
wife a push!

00:08:24.889 --> 00:08:29.110
But Baelish isn’t the sort of man who’d
just casually chuck you out the moon door

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:34.130
without a wily word or two on the matter.
No, he’s the kind of guy who likes to give

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:39.060
you something to think about as you’re hurtling
through the air to certain death.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:44.690
And so it was with Lysa, whose face was an
absolute picture of love as Littlefinger told

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:49.510
her he’d only ever loved one woman, but
that look on Lysa’s face soon changed to

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:55.050
one of horror as he revealed he actually meant
her sister, Catelyn!

00:08:55.050 --> 00:09:02.050
It was a surprise for book-readers and non-book-readers
when Jojen met his grabby, stabby, icy, firey

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.990
end in the season 4 finale.
The Bran clan were on their way to meet the

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:12.200
3-Eyed Raven when they were attacked by an
army of skeleton wights who emerged mysteriously

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.930
from beneath the snow!
Jojen’s sister Meera tried to fight off

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:20.180
the gruesome creatures as did Hodor, who Bran
warged into.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:25.650
But as a sickly Jojen lay on the ground, a
headless wight stabbed him repeatedly in the

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:28.150
stomach.
Meera lopped its arm off, but the damage was

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:32.280
already done, and there was nothing to do
but put her brother out of his misery with

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:37.020
a quick cut to the throat.
And, as you can never be dead enough in the

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:42.630
GOT world, the female Child of the Forest
firebombed Jojen to smithereens, ensuring

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:47.110
he couldn’t be reanimated.
I loved the drama of this scene, including

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:50.310
the wights’ hands suddenly reaching out
of the snow.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:56.320
It was a bit like Ray Harryhausen meets Michael
Jackson’s Thriller video!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:01.210
When Bronn decided not to champion Tyrion
in his trial by combat, and instead chose

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:07.860
social climbing over what was basically a
suicide mission, Dornish man of the moment

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.330
Oberyn Martell stood up and volunteered his
services.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:15.790
Of course, there was a little more to it than
that as Oberyn was desperate for the chance

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:20.850
to kill his sister Elia’s murderer, Gregor
Clegane, and drag a confession out of him

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:25.740
before he died.
Err, well, that didn’t all exactly go to

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:31.690
plan: he did get the confession, but only
as he was being given a mind-blowing headache

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.930
and having his eyes gouged out by the Mountain.
Nice!

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:39.760
I don’t think there’s any question that
this was the most horrifying death of season

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.140
4 – in terms of the way it was executed
and how we felt about Oberyn and Gregor.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:48.270
So, what do you think were the best deaths
in season 4 of Game of Thrones?

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:53.490
Let me know in the comments below!
Honourable mentions go to Shae, Pyp, Dontos

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:57.720
Hollard, and the Meereenese champion dispatched
by Daario Naharis.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.620
If you like this video, hit the thumbs up
button and don’t forget to subscribe so

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:06.850
you don’t miss out on more top 10s coming
up, as well as season 5 episode reviews and

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:10.650
exclusive cast interviews.
And remember, if you’re not watching Jan

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:13.399
G on GoT, you know nothing!

